---
import bg_praise from '../assets/bg_praise2.jpg'
---
<section class="quotes" id="reviews">
  <div class="praise_title">Advanced Praise for: <span style="font-style:italic;">the ART of</span> TRUE ADVANTAGE</div>
  
  <div class="slider-container">
    <button class="nav-btn prev" id="prevBtn">❮</button>
    
    <div class="quote-overflow">
      <div class="quote-track" id="quoteTrack">
        
        <div class="quote-card" data-index="0" title="Click to read full review">
          <div class="quote-body">
            <p class="clamped-quote">“The Art of True Advantage: Best Practices for Optimal Outcomes is an outstanding new resource for continuing to become your best self. Its author, Christopher Boyer, is one of the best leadership self-realization growth teachers that I have ever seen and been inspired by. His ability and capabilities in lighting the path to personal leadership growth from the most abstract truths to the actionable “know hows” are extraordinary. [...]”</p>
            <span class="read-more">Read full review ➜</span>
          </div>
          <div class="quote-footer">
            <hr>
            <p class="author-name">Dr. William A. Korach</p>
            <p class="author-title">Retired Superintendent of Schools, Lake Oswego, OR; PSU Resident Professor</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="quote-card" data-index="1" title="Click to read full review">
          <div class="quote-body">
            <p class="clamped-quote">“The Art of True Advantage is not merely a collection of ideas—it is a complete system. It builds upon the foundation of awareness and creates continuous Kaizen cycles through each level of growth and development. This book provides a practical framework for anyone seeking mastery, self-awareness, and continual improvement. [...]”</p>
            <span class="read-more">Read full review ➜</span>
          </div>
          <div class="quote-footer">
            <hr>
            <p class="author-name">Cory Mahaffey</p>
            <p class="author-title">Founder and Managing Partner</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="quote-card" data-index="2" title="Click to read full review">
          <div class="quote-body">
            <p class="clamped-quote">“There are books that inform, and there are books that shape the way you operate. The Art of True Advantage falls decisively into the latter. In many ways, the author carries forward a tradition that traces back to ancient thinkers, individuals who understood that the foundation of external success is internal discipline. [...]”</p>
            <span class="read-more">Read full review ➜</span>
          </div>
          <div class="quote-footer">
            <hr>
            <p class="author-name">Bryan Welton</p>
            <p class="author-title">Founder, Investor & Entrepreneur</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="quote-card" data-index="3" title="Click to read full review">
          <div class="quote-body">
            <p class="clamped-quote">“This book feels less like something you read and more like something you experience, quietly, deeply, and in ways that linger long after you’ve turned the final page. It doesn’t overwhelm you with complicated theories or abstract philosophies. Instead, it walks beside you, step by step, offering simple, clear guidance. [...]”</p>
            <span class="read-more">Read full review ➜</span>
          </div>
          <div class="quote-footer">
            <hr>
            <p class="author-name">Paul Terrell</p>
            <p class="author-title">Adjunct Professor Portland State University</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="quote-card" data-index="4" title="Click to read full review">
          <div class="quote-body">
            <p class="clamped-quote">“Christopher Boyer has created a compendium of valuable lessons available to all of us based on his lifetime devotion to the betterment of humanity. He has amplified the intellectual and behavioral skills of martial arts reflected in outcomes of respect and resilience. This material is both informational and instructional. [...]”</p>
            <span class="read-more">Read full review ➜</span>
          </div>
          <div class="quote-footer">
            <hr>
            <p class="author-name">Edward L. Brewington</p>
            <p class="author-title">Retired Senior VP, Educator, Black Belt</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="quote-card" data-index="5" title="Click to read full review">
          <div class="quote-body">
            <p class="clamped-quote">“What this book does well is close the gap between intention and action. It forces an honest look at distraction, misplaced emotion, and avoidance. Then it offers a path forward. Pay attention to what matters. Act on it consistently. That is not just productivity. That is stewardship of what you have been given. [...]”</p>
            <span class="read-more">Read full review ➜</span>
          </div>
          <div class="quote-footer">
            <hr>
            <p class="author-name">Gary Hanifan</p>
            <p class="author-title">Former Senior Managing Director Accenture Strategy</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <button class="nav-btn next" id="nextBtn">❯</button>
  </div>

  <div class="modal-overlay" id="quoteModal">
    <div class="modal-content-wrapper">
      <button class="modal-close" id="modalClose">✕</button>
      
      <div class="modal-nav-container">
        <button class="nav-btn modal-arrow" id="modalPrev">❮</button>
        
        <div class="modal-body" id="modalBody"></div>
        
        <button class="nav-btn modal-arrow" id="modalNext">❯</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .quotes {
    --bg-image: url('../assets/bg_praise2.jpg');
    position: relative;
    padding: 100px 20px;
    min-height: 90vh;
    color: white;
    text-align: center;
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box; 
    scroll-margin-top: 80px;
    overflow: hidden;
    z-index: 1;
    /* RE-ENABLED: Restores standard desktop parallax background layer */
    background: var(--bg-image) no-repeat center 10% / cover fixed;
  }

  .quotes::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    /* FIX: Set Y-axis to 20% to nudge the frame down and prevent chopping heads */
    background: var(--bg-image) no-repeat center 35% / cover fixed;
    filter: blur(4px); 
    /* transform: scale(1.04);  */
    z-index: -1; 
  }

  .praise_title {
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 60px;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
    word-wrap: break-word; 
  }

  .slider-container {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    position: relative;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .quote-overflow {
    overflow: hidden;
    width: 100%;
    padding-top: 15px;
    padding-bottom: 15px;
    margin-top: -15px;
    margin-bottom: -15px;
  }

  .quote-track {
    display: flex;
    transition: transform 0.6s ease-in-out;
    gap: 20px;
    align-items: stretch; 
  }

  .quote-card {
    min-width: calc(33.33% - 14px);
    min-height: 480px;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6); 
    backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
    padding: 40px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(215, 137, 65, 0.3);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    text-align: left;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: transform 0.2s, border-color 0.2s;
  }

  .quote-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-5px); 
    border-color: rgba(215, 137, 65, 0.8);
  }

  .clamped-quote {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-style: italic;
    display: -webkit-box;
    -webkit-line-clamp: 9; 
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .read-more {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: #d78941;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    display: block;
    margin-top: 10px;
  }

  .author-name {
    margin-top: 15px;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-style: normal !important;
    color: #d78941;
    text-shadow: 1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.8); 
  }

  .author-title {
    font-size: 0.9rem !important;
    font-style: normal !important;
    color: #e0e0e0;
  }

  .nav-btn {
    background: rgba(215, 137, 65, 0.8);
    border: none;
    color: white;
    padding: 15px;
    cursor: pointer;
    border-radius: 50%;
    margin: 0 10px;
    z-index: 10;
    transition: scale 0.2s;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 50px;
    height: 50px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .nav-btn:hover {
    scale: 1.1;
    background: #d78941;
  }

  hr {
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);
    margin: 20px 0;
  }

  /* MODAL STYLES */
  .modal-overlay {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85);
    backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
    z-index: 99999; 
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    transition: opacity 0.3s ease;
  }

  .modal-overlay.active {
    opacity: 1;
    pointer-events: all;
  }

  .modal-content-wrapper {
    position: relative;
    width: 90%;
    max-width: 900px;
    max-height: 70vh; 
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column; 
    background: #111;
    border: 1px solid #d78941;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 40px 20px 20px 20px;
    box-shadow: 0 15px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
  }

  .modal-nav-container {
    display: flex;
    align-items: stretch; 
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    flex-grow: 1;
    min-height: 0; 
  }

  .nav-btn.modal-arrow {
    align-self: center;
  }

  .modal-body {
    flex-grow: 1;
    overflow-y: auto; 
    min-height: 0; 
    text-align: left;
    color: #fff;
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    padding: 0 15px 15px 0; 
  }

  .modal-body::-webkit-scrollbar {
    width: 6px;
  }
  .modal-body::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .modal-body::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
    background: rgba(215, 137, 65, 0.5);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .modal-body::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {
    background: rgba(215, 137, 65, 0.9);
  }

  .modal-body .author-name {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .modal-close {
    position: absolute;
    top: 10px;
    right: 15px;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: color 0.2s;
    z-index: 10;
  }

  .modal-close:hover {
    color: #d78941;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1200px) {
    .quote-card { min-width: calc(50% - 10px); }
  }

  /* --- MOBILE SPECIFIC CSS --- */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    /* MOBILE FIX: Syncs layout, locks background shift, disables parallax on tiny viewports */
    #reviews::before {
      background-size: auto 115% !important;
      background-position: 60% 60% !important; 
      background-attachment: scroll !important; /* Forces scroll processing to avoid rendering errors on iOS/Android */
    }

    .quotes {
      min-height: auto !important; /* Allows content to define height on mobile */;
      padding: 60px 15px;
    }

    .clamped-quote {
      -webkit-line-clamp: 7 !important; /* Forces a maximum of 6 lines on mobile */
    }

    .praise_title {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 30px;
    }
    
    .quote-card { 
      min-width: 100%; 
      min-height: 0 !important;
      height: auto !important;
      padding: 24px 20px; 
    }
    
    .nav-btn {
      width: 40px; 
      height: 40px; 
      margin: 0 5px; 
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }

    .modal-content-wrapper {
      width: 92%;
      padding: 45px 15px 20px 15px; 
      max-height: 65vh; 
      box-sizing: border-box; 
    }
    
    .modal-nav-container { 
      display: grid; 
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      grid-template-rows: 1fr auto; 
      gap: 15px;
      min-height: 0; 
    }
    
    .modal-body { 
      grid-column: 1 / -1; 
      grid-row: 1; 
      margin-top: 5px; 
      padding-right: 5px; 
    }
    
    .nav-btn.modal-arrow { 
      display: flex; 
      position: static; 
      margin: 0;
      width: 45px;
      height: 45px;
      justify-self: center; 
    }

    #modalPrev { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 2; }
    #modalNext { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 2; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Slider Logic
  const track = document.getElementById('quoteTrack');
  const cards = document.querySelectorAll('.quote-card');
  const nextBtn = document.getElementById('nextBtn');
  const prevBtn = document.getElementById('prevBtn');
  
  let sliderIndex = 0;
  const totalCards = cards.length;
  
  function getVisibleCards() {
    if (window.innerWidth > 1200) return 3;
    if (window.innerWidth > 768) return 2;
    return 1;
  }

  function updateSlider() {
    const visibleCards = getVisibleCards();
    const maxIndex = totalCards - visibleCards;
    
    if (sliderIndex > maxIndex) sliderIndex = maxIndex;
    if (sliderIndex < 0) sliderIndex = 0;

    const cardWidth = cards[0].offsetWidth + 20; 
    track.style.transform = `translateX(-${sliderIndex * cardWidth}px)`;
  }

  nextBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const maxIndex = totalCards - getVisibleCards();
    sliderIndex = (sliderIndex >= maxIndex) ? 0 : sliderIndex + 1;
    updateSlider();
  });

  prevBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const maxIndex = totalCards - getVisibleCards();
    sliderIndex = (sliderIndex <= 0) ? maxIndex : sliderIndex - 1;
    updateSlider();
  });

  let autoRotate = setInterval(() => { nextBtn.click(); }, 20000);

  window.addEventListener('resize', updateSlider);

  // Modal Logic
  const fullQuotes = [
    `“The Art of True Advantage: Best Practices for Optimal Outcomes is an outstanding new resource for continuing to become your best self. Its author, Christopher Boyer, is one of the best leadership self-realization growth teachers that I have ever seen and been inspired by. His ability and capabilities in lighting the path to personal leadership growth from the most abstract truths to the actionable “know hows” are extraordinary. Now he has written a must have book for anyone who wants to continue learning through best practices.<br><br>The breadth and depth of the advantages he identifies and explains in detail, including the process steps that need to be undertaken and developed, are meaningful, clear and enhanced by quotes from well-known people sharing their wisdom. Having taught over 50 Leadership classes at Lewis and Clark and Portland State Universities combined, I would make The Art of True Advantage: Best Practices for Optimal Outcomes required reading for my students and recommend it to anyone who has a strong desire to continue learning and bettering who they are capable of being.”<br><br><span class="author-name">Dr. William A. Korach</span><br><span class="author-title">Retired Superintendent of Schools, Lake Oswego, OR; PSU Resident Professor</span>`,
    
    `“The Art of True Advantage is not merely a collection of ideas—it is a complete system. It builds upon the foundation of awareness and creates continuous Kaizen cycles through each level of growth and development. This book provides a practical framework for anyone seeking mastery, self-awareness, and continual improvement.<br><br>Christopher has created more than a philosophy; he has built a system for mastery. His teachings on awareness, focus, and self-development are timeless, portable, and immediately applicable to leadership, parenting, business, and life. What begins as tactical insight quickly reveals itself to be transformational wisdom. The Art of True Advantage provides a framework for building awareness, creating continuous improvement, and becoming your best self in every arena of life.”<br><br><span class="author-name">Cory Mahaffey</span><br><span class="author-title">Founder and Managing Partner</span>`,
    
    `“There are books that inform, and there are books that shape the way you operate. The Art of True Advantage falls decisively into the latter.<br><br>In many ways, the author carries forward a tradition that traces back to ancient thinkers, individuals who understood that the foundation of external success is internal discipline. What Boyer has done, however, is something distinctly modern: he has organized those enduring principles into a practical, sequential system that can be applied in real time. That sequential structure is what makes this book exceptional.<br><br>This is not a book to be read once and placed on a shelf. It is something to return to often. The concepts are designed to be applied in the middle of real decisions, real conversations, and real pressure. Over time, they compound. And when they compound, they change not just outcomes, but identity.<br><br>From a leadership &amp; relationship perspective, this is where the real value emerges. Too often, leadership is framed externally in terms of strategy, communication and execution. This book begins where it should, with the individual, my state, my attention, my responsibility. These are not soft ideas; they are the foundation of consistent and incremental performance.<br><br>For anyone building a business or relationships, leading a team, or simply trying to function at a higher level of intention, this framework provides a clear path. It removes noise. It replaces complexity with discipline.<br><br>Ultimately, The Art of True Advantage is not about gaining an edge in a single area. It is about becoming the kind of person who consistently creates advantage in all aspects of life, across situations, over time, and under pressure, thereby strengthening self and subsequently, those around you.”<br><br><span class="author-name">Bryan Welton</span><br><span class="author-title">Founder, Investor &amp; Entrepreneur</span>`,
    
    `“This book feels less like something you read and more like something you experience, quietly, deeply, and in ways that linger long after you’ve turned the final page.<br><br>It doesn’t overwhelm you with complicated theories or abstract philosophies. Instead, it walks beside you, step by step, offering simple, clear guidance on how to live a fuller, kinder, more meaningful life. And somehow, in its simplicity, it becomes profound.<br><br>Every idea is grounded in everyday moments, the kind we all recognize but rarely pause to learn from.<br><br>By the end, you don’t feel like you’ve been instructed, you feel like you understand something new. You feel capable. You feel hopeful. There’s a softness to that realization, a kind of emotional clarity that sneaks up on you. After reading it, you walk away feeling just a little lighter, a little stronger, and a lot more ready to live your life fully and wholeheartedly.”<br><br><span class="author-name">Paul Terrell</span><br><span class="author-title">Adjunct Professor Portland State University</span>`,
    
    `“Christopher Boyer has created a compendium of valuable lessons available to all of us based on his lifetime devotion to the betterment of humanity. He has amplified the intellectual and behavioral skills of martial arts reflected in outcomes of respect and resilience. This material is both informational and instructional and presented in an easy to understand manner.”<br><br><span class="author-name">Edward L. Brewington</span><br><span class="author-title">Retired Senior VP, Educator, Black Belt</span>`,
    
    `“What this book does well is close the gap between intention and action. It forces an honest look at distraction, misplaced emotion, and avoidance. Then it offers a path forward. Pay attention to what matters. Act on it consistently. That is not just productivity. That is stewardship of what you have been given.<br><br>This is not about motivation. It is about rightly ordered vision. When attention and intention line up with reality, things change.<br><br>This is not a book you can hide in. It removes the easy outs and puts responsibility back where it belongs. Advantage is not something you find. It is something you build through attention, intention, and action. That kind of clarity feels a lot like an honest examen. No excuses. Just truth.”<br><br><span class="author-name">Gary Hanifan</span><br><span class="author-title">Former Senior Managing Director Accenture Strategy</span>`
  ];

  const modal = document.getElementById('quoteModal');
  const modalBody = document.getElementById('modalBody');
  const modalClose = document.getElementById('modalClose');
  const modalNext = document.getElementById('modalNext');
  const modalPrev = document.getElementById('modalPrev');
  
  let currentModalIndex = 0;

  function renderModalQuote() {
    modalBody.innerHTML = fullQuotes[currentModalIndex];
    modalBody.scrollTop = 0; 
  }

  function openModal(index) {
    currentModalIndex = parseInt(index, 10);
    renderModalQuote();
    modal.classList.add('active');
    clearInterval(autoRotate); 
  }

  function closeModal() {
    modal.classList.remove('active');
    autoRotate = setInterval(() => { nextBtn.click(); }, 20000);
  }

  cards.forEach(card => {
    card.addEventListener('click', () => {
      openModal(card.dataset.index);
    });
  });

  modalNext.addEventListener('click', () => {
    currentModalIndex = (currentModalIndex >= fullQuotes.length - 1) ? 0 : currentModalIndex + 1;
    renderModalQuote();
  });

  modalPrev.addEventListener('click', () => {
    currentModalIndex = (currentModalIndex <= 0) ? fullQuotes.length - 1 : currentModalIndex - 1;
    renderModalQuote();
  });

  modalClose.addEventListener('click', closeModal);
  modal.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    if (e.target === modal) closeModal(); 
  });
  document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
    if (e.key === 'Escape' && modal.classList.contains('active')) closeModal();
    if (e.key === 'ArrowRight' && modal.classList.contains('active')) modalNext.click();
    if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft' && modal.classList.contains('active')) modalPrev.click();
  });

  document.querySelectorAll('nav a, .nav-link, [href^="#"]').forEach(link => {
    link.addEventListener('click', () => {
      // Check if the modal is currently open before closing
      if (modal.classList.contains('active')) {
        closeModal();
      }
    });
  });
</script>